==Special Moves==
====Reppuu Ken====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=rock_236a,rock_236c,rock_236ac
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|display=200x200px
|description3=*C and AC version are two hit, the first hit can nullify a projectile and the second can go through the projectile.
Rock's grounded fireball that travels fullscreen.
----
'''A version''': Standard one hit fireball. Longer startup than the other version, but the fireball comes out faster and has less recovery. This makes it ideal for neutral and zoning situations compared to the other two.
----
'''C version''': The Double Reppuken. Rock leaves a small hitbox in front of him before firing a fireball. The first hit can destroy other fireballs, allowing the second to go through.<br>
Extremely slow compared to the A version, meaning you should save this for counter-zoning in fireball wars. Worth noting that Rock can also use this after a juggle into DP Brake in the corner to do 623C Brake > 236C > 623A/AC or 236236C/REV. While the timing is tight, and the follow-ups are limited due to the specific juggle, it's a good way to tack on extra damage without spending REV gauge. 
----
'''AC version''': An enhanced version of the C Double Reppuken, sharing its initial hitbox into fireball. Plus on block, allowing you to pressure reset with it.<br>
This version is very strong for REV chains, allowing you to use it before something like 214AC for a hit confirm that leaves you plus (at the cost of some REV) or in an extended juggle sequence, like 214BD~C, 236AC > 214BD~A. Note that in that juggle, you are linking 236AC, so your REV gauge cost will not be reduced.
}}

